WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.324
Every call recording and every voice media clip has to live somewhere.

00:00:05.324 --> 00:00:10.046
This short video shows where the platform keeps them, how they are protected,

00:00:10.046 --> 00:00:13.460
and how a company can move them to Azure Blob Storage.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.739
By default, call recordings, and the master copy of every voice media clip,

00:00:22.739 --> 00:00:26.610
are kept in a folder of the site, and every file is encrypted

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.169
before it is written.

00:00:28.169 --> 00:00:31.000
The same store serves every phone provider.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.563
The phone provider records the call on its side.

00:00:34.563 --> 00:00:39.251
The platform downloads the finished recording into the store, so the recording stays

00:00:39.251 --> 00:00:41.230
with you if you change provider.

00:00:45.418 --> 00:00:50.678
Listen to recordings on Interaction Center, Call recordings, which you reach with the

00:00:50.678 --> 00:00:54.377
permission to listen to your own, or anyone's, recordings.

00:00:54.377 --> 00:00:59.118
Here there are no recordings, because no call can connect on this demo site.

00:00:59.574 --> 00:01:03.444
Voice media clips keep their master copy in the same store.

00:01:03.444 --> 00:01:06.719
Open Interaction Center, Management, Voice Media:

00:01:06.719 --> 00:01:11.006
the badges show whether a clip has its master copy and whether the

00:01:11.006 --> 00:01:12.674
provider holds a copy.

00:01:16.974 --> 00:01:21.453
To keep them in Azure Blob Storage instead, turn on the feature Telephony,

00:01:21.453 --> 00:01:24.980
Azure Blob Storage, which you find under Tools, Features.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:27.724
It changes only where the files are stored.

00:01:28.176 --> 00:01:32.621
Your developer supplies the storage account in the site's configuration.

00:01:32.621 --> 00:01:37.636
Until that is done, the feature changes nothing, and the local store stays in use.

00:01:38.086 --> 00:01:43.209
Recordings are still encrypted with the site's own key before they leave the

00:01:43.209 --> 00:01:46.208
site, so Azure only holds scrambled files.

00:01:46.208 --> 00:01:51.456
Recording rules, pausing, deletion and the audit trail are the same as before.

00:01:55.656 --> 00:02:00.896
Deleting a voice media clip deletes its master copy and every provider copy.

00:02:00.896 --> 00:02:05.817
If two environments share one store, deleting a clip in one removes the

00:02:05.817 --> 00:02:07.606
audio the other plays.

00:02:08.356 --> 00:02:14.067
Deleting a recording erases its file, and a recording under legal hold cannot be deleted.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:18.936
Only an administrator holds the permission to delete recordings by default.

00:02:20.936 --> 00:02:24.192
By default recordings stay encrypted on the site.

00:02:24.192 --> 00:02:29.047
Azure Blob Storage moves the same encrypted files, and nothing else changes.

00:02:29.047 --> 00:02:30.586
Thanks for watching.

